      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:34:3",
      "text": [
        " كَانَ عَلِيٌّ ( صلوات الله عليه ) يَقُولُ لِوُلْدِهِ يَا بَنِيَّ انْظُرُوا بَيْتَ رَبِّكُمْ فَلَا يَخْلُوَنَّ مِنْكُمْ فَلَا تُنَاظَرُوا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Al Hajjal, from Hammad, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Ali<sup>asws</sup> was saying to his<sup>asws</sup> sons: ‘O my<sup>asws</sup> sons! Consider the House (Kabah) of your Lord<sup>azwj</sup>, so it should not be empty from you, and never have conflict (second thoughts) about (visiting it)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from al-Hajjal from Hammad who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said that ’Amir al-Mu’minin would say to his sons, ‘My sons, take the House of your Lord in your consideration so it is not left without your presence therein; otherwise, you will risk coming of torment upon you.”’ "
        ]
      }
    },
